% Demo corpus 1 (D10) — human-readable TRL source for the dogfood FAQ about TRUGS
% and this chatbot. The executable artifact is faq.trug.json (trug validate-VALID);
% this file is the readable companion. Each answer below is delivered verbatim by the
% engine at its leaf, with the node-id path as a provenance address.

PARTY user MAY ASK ABOUT TOPIC trugs OR TOPIC engine OR TOPIC crypto.

% root → what_is_trugs (answer)
PROCESS engine SHALL DELIVER ANSWER what_is_trugs
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT TOPIC trugs.

% root → engine (branch) → { how_it_walks, what_is_bottom, why_no_hallucination }
PROCESS engine SHALL OFFER MENU engine
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT TOPIC engine.
PROCESS engine SHALL DELIVER ANSWER how_it_walks
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT RECORD selection.
PROCESS engine SHALL DELIVER ANSWER what_is_bottom
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT RECORD bottom.
PROCESS engine SHALL DELIVER ANSWER why_no_hallucination
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT RECORD hallucination.

% root → crypto (answer) — honest transport-scope claim, never Signal-parity
PROCESS engine SHALL DELIVER ANSWER crypto
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT TOPIC crypto.

% Every menu falls through to an authored bottom (root_none / engine_none): a miss is
% located and recorded, never silently composed.
PROCESS engine SHALL RETURN RECORD bottom_route
  WHEN PARTY user ASK ABOUT ANY OTHER TOPIC.
